# Atomic design

UI lives in `components/{atoms,molecules,organisms,templates}`. `app/` only assembles pages.

| Layer | Rule | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| `atoms/` | One job. No other unhash components. | `Button`, `Hash`, `Amount`, `Note`, `TextInput` |
| `molecules/` | A few atoms with one purpose. | `Account`, `Fact`, `HashInput`, `SiteHeader` |
| `organisms/` | A whole section. | `Narrative`, `StoryView` |
| `templates/` | Page chrome / layout slots. | `Shell` |
| `app/` | Routes. No shared UI definitions. | `page.tsx`, `tx/[hash]/page.tsx` |

- New UI goes in the **lowest** layer that fits. Do not drop a molecule in `app/` or an atom in `organisms/`.
- Import from the layer barrel (`@/components/atoms`) except `"use client"` files — import those by path (`@/components/molecules/HashInput`) so server barrels stay server.
- A layer may import only from layers below it: templates → organisms → molecules → atoms → `lib/`.
- Compose. Do not copy an atom's className stack into a higher layer.
